[size=5][b]More Map Markers[/b][/size]

Raises the limit on custom markers you can place on the PDA map. The vanilla game only allows [b]10[/b].

Made for the [url=https://forums.nexusmods.com/topic/13502974-mod-request-stalker-2-more-player-markers-on-map/]mod request on the Nexus forums[/url], so you can tag every artifact anomaly, stash and point of interest you come across.

[size=4][b]Versions[/b][/size]
Pick [b]one[/b]:
[list]
[*][b]50[/b] markers
[*][b]99[/b] markers [i](recommended: still fits the PDA's marker counter)[/i]
[*][b]999[/b] markers
[/list]
Need a different number? The [url=https://github.com/la2o/stalker2-moremapmarkers]source repository[/url] has a script that builds any limit from your own game files.

[size=4][b]How is this different from other marker limit mods?[/b][/size]
[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stalker2heartofchornobyl/mods/1442]Change User Markers Limit[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stalker2heartofchornobyl/mods/2466]Map Markers Unlimited[/url] raise the same limit. They ship a copy of the map settings asset from the game version they were made for: patch 1.7 and 2.0.6 respectively. This mod:
[list]
[*]Is built from and tested on the current game version (October 2026). In current versions the asset no longer stores the limit at all, so the mod adds it back rather than editing an existing value.
[*]Is open source. The build script makes the mod from your own game files, so after a game patch anyone can rebuild it right away instead of waiting for an update.
[*]Isn't limited to 50, 99 or 999: the script builds any limit you want.
[/list]
Install only one marker limit mod at a time.

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[b]Manual:[/b] extract the archive into your game folder (the one that contains [font=Courier New]Stalker2[/font]). You should end up with three files ([font=Courier New].pak[/font], [font=Courier New].utoc[/font] and [font=Courier New].ucas[/font]) in:
[code]Stalker2/Content/Paks/~mods/[/code]
[b]Uninstall:[/b] delete those three files.

Only install one version at a time.

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Overrides [font=Courier New]/Game/GameLite/FPS_Game/UIRemaster/PDA/WorldMap/MapSettingsAsset[/font]. Any other mod that changes this asset (including other marker limit mods) will conflict with this one.
[*]No [font=Courier New].cfg[/font] files are touched, so it works alongside config mods.
[*]If a game patch changes the map settings asset, this mod may need a rebuild.
[/list]

[size=4][b]How it works[/b][/size]
The marker limit isn't a config value. It's an integer stored on the PDA map settings asset. This mod repacks that asset from the game with the new limit, using a packer written from scratch ([url=https://github.com/la2o/stalker2-moremapmarkers]source[/url]).
